  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform $\\operatorname{rod} A B$ is suspended from a point $X$, at a variable distance from $x$ from $A$, as shown. To make the rod horizontal, a mass $m$ is suspended from its end $A$. A set of $(m, x)$ values is recorded. The appropriate variable that give a straight line, when plotted, are:\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/rIP-BGVAb1_-v4HYRf1xB_mxLmzinV9eiF6UvRl6Hbw.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LXwHA",
      "text": "\n$m, \\frac{1}{x}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "4BBPV",
      "text": "\n$m, \\frac{1}{x^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iZ7eF",
      "text": "\n$m, x$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4dxNe",
      "text": "\n$m, x^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Balancing torque w.r.t. point of suspension\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&m g x=M g\\left(\\frac{\\ell}{2}-x\\right) \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow m x=M \\frac{\\ell}{2}-M x \\\\\n&m=\\left(M \\frac{\\ell}{2}\\right) \\frac{1}{x}-M\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0Xf_q1ovlKrEiOlIK6TYQCc7pVwWPRhKOpXJ76UqdLA.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$y=\\alpha \\frac{1}{x}-C \\quad$ Straight line equation.",
    "image": null
  },
